  "body": "Part of #1445.\n\nToday's Back bore cycle feeds out (G89's shape) but forces the dwell to 0 and feeds out at the cutting feed, while the canned word carries one F for both directions. #1445 asks for dwell at depth on the feed-out cycles too.\n\nWhat is owed:\n- Let the Back bore (G89) cycle carry the user's dwell, and decide (decision entry) whether its feed out should use the plunge feed so the chain matches the single F word the canned cycle posts.\n- Read the dwell unit per post: Fanuc-family posts here write P as integer milliseconds, grblHAL and Tormach as seconds. Pin each touched post's P word with a golden; a post whose dwell unit is not stated refuses a dwell by name instead of guessing.\n- Programs that do not set a dwell post byte-identical (existing goldens unchanged).\n\nDone means: a G89 with a dwell posts the right P in each canned post (pinned per post), the CL chain the verifier reads matches what the control runs, and the unit is never guessed.\n",
